The body-sensitivity check also behaved correctly: the mutated definition compiled, but the unchanged theorem exited 1 with a stuck equality between the original count and count-plus-one. The remaining issue is adequacy, not soundness: the K proof executes the exact translated implementation and returns a constrained arithmetic summary, but the spec never machine-connects that summary to the original “count all valid triples” definition; its three residue lemmas are separate and unused by the main claim.
